    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes CI failure that has existed on `main` since **ADR-034's implementation merged (#179)**. One-line dependency gap + defensive verification.\n\n## The bug\n\nCI fails at CMake configure with:\n\n```\n-- Checking for module 'librsvg-2.0'\n--   Package 'librsvg-2.0' not found\nCMake Error: The following required packages were not found:\n  - librsvg-2.0\n  CMakeLists.txt:57 (pkg_check_modules)\n```\n\n`.github/workflows/build.yml` installs `libgtkmm-4.0-dev` and `libcurl4-openssl-dev` but not `librsvg2-dev`. ADR-034 introduced the librsvg dependency in `CMakeLists.txt:57` on 2026-10-27.\n\n### Affected runs\n\n| PR | Branch | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| #177 (docs) | `docs/adr-034-img-absolute` | ✅ (before librsvg added) |\n| #178 (docs) | `docs/adr-034-svg-amendment` | ✅ (before librsvg added) |\n| **#179 (impl)** | `feat/img-absolute` | **❌ (librsvg added here)** |\n| #180 (docs) | `docs/adr-034-implemented` | ❌ (inherits broken CI) |\n| **#181 (url fix)** | `fix/protocol-relative-url` | **❌ (still broken)** |\n\nLocal builds passed all through (developer machine has `librsvg2-dev`). CI failed at configure in ~36-41 seconds.\n\n## The fix\n\n```yaml\nsudo apt-get install -y \\\n  build-essential \\\n  cmake \\\n  ninja-build \\\n  pkg-config \\\n  libgtkmm-4.0-dev \\\n  libcurl4-openssl-dev \\\n  librsvg2-dev          # ADR-034 dependency\n```\n\nPlus: expand the existing \"Verify GTK 4 bindings\" step to verify **all five** pkg-config modules the CMakeLists requires:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Verify CMake pkg-config dependencies\n  run: |\n    pkg-config --modversion gtkmm-4.0\n    pkg-config --modversion libcurl\n    pkg-config --modversion cairo\n    pkg-config --modversion pangocairo\n    pkg-config --modversion librsvg-2.0\n```\n\nFuture missing-dependency breakage now fails at a clearly named step (\"Verify CMake pkg-config dependencies\") with a specific pkg-config error, not buried in CMake configure output.\n\n## The discipline gap, honestly\n\nThe \"merged cleanly\" signal in this session's ADR-034 cycle was **local-only**. Local builds pass 421/1737; CI has been failing silently since #179 merged. The signal \"everything's fine\" was measuring the wrong subsystem — exactly the pattern ADR-028 identified (\"a subsystem's local tests can pass while the subsystem is never reached in production\"), but worse: this time the subsystem is CI itself.\n\nCorrection sequence:\n1. **This PR**: fix workflow, prove CI green\n2. **Follow-up docs PR**: record the correction in ADR-034's Implementation section (Post-Implementation Note, 2026-10-27)\n\nSame discipline as every prior correction in the arc's record: the original claim stays (PR #179 and #181 merged as commits), the correction is added alongside. First correction pattern that's about the **verification methodology** itself, not a feature.\n\n## Test plan\n\nThis PR's own CI run IS the test:\n- **Green** → workflow fix works, `main` will go green on merge\n- **Red** → more than one dependency missing; expand apt-get\n- **Red (other reason)** → not this PR; needs investigation\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Expected |\n|---|---|\n| PR's own CI run passes | (this PR proves itself) |\n| `main` CI green after merge | verified by follow-up `gh run list` |\n| Local build still passes | 421 / 1737 unchanged |\n\nRefs ADR-034\n",
